      <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
        <div class="faq-question" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
          How does InOro integrate with our telephony system?
          <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          InOro connects via API, SFTP, or batch file upload. We have native connectors for common platforms (Genesys, Avaya, Cisco, Amazon Connect) and can handle custom formats. If you have an existing recording storage — on-prem, cloud, or a vendor's system — we can work with it. Integrations are discussed during onboarding.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
        <div class="faq-question" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
          How long does implementation take?
          <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          A pilot on your existing recordings is typically ready in 5–7 business days. Full production deployment depends on your integration setup, but most clients are operational within 2–4 weeks. There's no required changes to your telephony infrastructure.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
        <div class="faq-question" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
          Where is data stored? Is it GDPR compliant?
          <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          All data is processed and stored within the EU. InOro is built GDPR by design — no data is transferred outside the EU. For regulated industries (BFSI, DORA-covered entities), InOro can also deploy in your own cloud or on-premise environment.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
        <div class="faq-question" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
          What languages are supported?
          <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Currently PL, EN, and DE with high accuracy. Other CEE languages (Czech, Slovak, Romanian) are supported with growing model quality. If your language isn't listed, ask us — we actively expand coverage based on demand.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
        <div class="faq-question" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
          Is there a minimum number of agents or calls?
          <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          No. Pricing is per minute processed — you pay for actual usage, nothing more. There's no minimum seat count, no minimum call volume, and no platform fees. Clients can start small and scale up as volume grows.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
        <div class="faq-question" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
          How is InOro different from Gong or Observe.AI?
          <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Gong is built for B2B sales calls — it doesn't handle contact center operations, compliance tracking, or BPO white-labeling. Observe.AI targets US enterprise customers with 100+ agent minimums and US-hosted infrastructure. InOro is built specifically for EU contact centers and BPO operations: EU-native hosting, CEE language models, full white-label capability, per-minute pricing with no minimums, and compliance features designed for European regulatory environments.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
        <div class="faq-question" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false">
          Can we test before committing?
          <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
